      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "despite the obvious segregation issue the problem with the system like this is that if you've spent even a little bit in time you'd realize that honestly rank really means nothing as far as the behavior of an individual. I've had a new users crash me I've had trusted users crash me I've met new users who are absolutely friendly I've met trusted users were absolutely friendly and everything in between. pretty much at this point the only thing the trust system really signifies is how long someone has played the game.\n\nhonestly at this point pretty much the only people I meet who even have the system turned on anymore are just using it as a sort of performance system to just generally disable stuff to help their frame rate",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
